{"results":[{"url":"https://www.livemint.com/news/world/us-gdp-surges-33-1-in-q3-biggest-gain-on-record-says-govt-11603976353011.html","final_url":"https://www.livemint.com/news/world/us-gdp-surges-33-1-in-q3-biggest-gain-on-record-says-govt-11603976353011.html","title":"US GDP surges 33.1% in Q3, biggest gain on record, says govt","description":"That came after a 31.4 percent drop in the April-June period during the worst of the Covid-19 pandemic, and a five percent drop in the first quarter","language":"en","text":"View Market Dashboard\n\n# US GDP surges 33.1% in Q3, biggest gain on record, says govt\n\n## That came after a 31.4 percent drop in the April-June period during the worst of the Covid-19 pandemic, and a five percent drop in the first quarter\n\nAFP\n\nUpdated29 Oct 2020, 06:31 PM IST\n\nPrefer Liveminton Google\n\n(Photo: AP)\n\nAfter the worst downturn on record, the US economy posted the strongest recovery on record as it expanded at a 33.1 percent annual rate in the third quarter, the Commerce Department reported Thursday.\n\nThat came after a 31.4 percent drop in the April-June period during the worst of the Covid-19 pandemic, and a five percent drop in the first quarter. The annual rate is a measure that shows the full-year result if the gain in a single quarter were translated over 12 months.\n\nHowever, compared to the July-September stretch of 2019, the third quarter contracted 2.9 percent after falling 9.0 percent year-over-year in the second quarter, according to the data, the first estimate of the results in the latest three months.\n\n\"The increase in third quarter GDP reflected continued efforts to reopen businesses and resume activities that were postponed or restricted due to COVID-19,\" the Commerce Department said in the release. It noted, however, that the \"full economic effects\" of the coronavirus cannot be separately measured.\n\nThe massive gain -- the biggest since record-keeping started in 1947 -- was driven by a surge in spending by consumers and businesses.\n\nBut economists warn that much of that was fueled by the massive $3 trillion in government aid that flooded the economy in the early weeks of the pandemic.\n\nMuch of that funding to jobless workers and businesses has run out, and other data show spending tapered off in September and the recovery is losing momentum.\n\nAnd the gain in the latest quarter was offset by a drop in government spending: federal government spending dropped 6.2 percent and state and local government fell 3.3 percent.\n\nStay updated with the latest Trending, India, World, CJP Protest in Delh LIVE and US news.\n\nHomeNewsWorldUS GDP surges 33.1% in Q3, biggest gain on record, says govt\n\nMore\n\n✕\n\n#### Wait for it…\n\nLog in to our website to save your bookmarks. It'll just take a moment.\n\n✕\n\n#### Wait for it…\n\nOops! Looks like you have exceeded the limit to bookmark the image. Remove some to bookmark this image.","author":"list.metadata.agency","published_date":"2020-10-29T18:31:52+05:30","latency_ms":241.87620499924378,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}